{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01NzL2gYZqw27gnJwsHggd3e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge from reference behavior on edge cases. This project runs a four-stage pipeline: extract (C source) → specify (PRDs via human) → synthesize (mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go) → verify (differential tests against Homebrew GNU binaries).\n\n**Architecture major components**:\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (runs Go binary vs GNU reference binary)\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — shared output formatting (tables, ANSI colors, sizes)\n- `cmd/<utility>/` — one Go package per utility\n- `magefiles/` — Mage build targets; the human↔orchestrator handoff boundary\n- `docs/` — human-authored specs; generation pipeline reads but never writes here\n\n**Current state**: Specs complete for ts, wc, cat, sponge, ls (core+extended), du, pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format. Code exists at `generation-merged` tags for those packages but the working branch (`generation-gh-262-codegen`) is clean with no generated code. Two consistency errors: orphaned PRDs prd012-true and prd013-false.\n\n**Current release — 00.0 (Batch 0, foundational infrastructure)**:\n- rel00.0-uc001-magefiles: spec_complete, code not started (generation target: cmd/version per DD7)\n- rel00.0-uc002-format: spec implemented, code not started (target: pkg/format)\n- rel00.0-uc003-sys: spec_complete, code not started (target: pkg/sys)\n- rel00.0-uc004-testutils: spec_complete, code not started (target: pkg/testutils)\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nAll four release 00.0 use cases have code not started. Applying P8 canonical ordering within the release:\n\n- Libraries and shared packages before consumers: pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils are all shared libraries; cmd/version is a consumer. Libraries go first.\n- Among the three libraries, there are no inter-dependencies (format does not need sys; testutils does not need format). Break the tie alphabetically by primary file path: `pkg/format` < `pkg/sys` < `pkg/testutils`.\n\nSingle task for this session: **pkg/format** (rel00.0-uc002-format).\n\n## Step 4: Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format output formatting library (rel00.0-uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format component description, technology_choices, design decisions DD3 and DD7)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate and read the PRD for pkg/format -- glob for prd*-format.yaml or prd*-pkg-format.yaml in this directory)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/table.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment for tabular output; rename file to match primary exported type from PRD if different\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI color codes for file type and permission display; rename to match PRD\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable byte size formatting; rename to match PRD\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement column alignment for tabular output (ls -l style) per the pkg/format PRD requirements\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement ANSI color code support for file types (directory, symlink, executable) and permissions per the pkg/format PRD requirements\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement human-readable size formatting that converts byte counts to K/M/G units per the pkg/format PRD requirements\n      - id: R4\n        text: All exported identifiers are idiomatic Go and the package compiles without warnings under golangci-lint\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Name each source file after its primary exported type, not the package name -- if the PRD specifies concrete type names (e.g. the primary type is Table, the file is table.go), use those and discard the suggested names above\n      - id: D2\n        text: pkg/format is a shared library consumed by cmd/ packages; it must not import from cmd/ or pkg/testutils\n      - id: D3\n        text: Do not use external Go packages for ANSI color output -- implement using string constants for ANSI escape sequences; the only permitted external dependency in the project is golang.org/x/sys per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology choices\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./pkg/format/ succeeds with no compilation errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: golangci-lint runs clean on all files under pkg/format/\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Column alignment function aligns each column to the maximum width of values in that column across all rows\n      - id: AC4\n        text: ANSI color escape sequences can be applied to and cleared from file-type label strings (directory, symlink, executable at minimum)\n      - id: AC5\n        text: Size formatting produces human-readable output using powers of 1024 (K=1024, M=1048576, G=1073741824) matching GNU coreutils human-readable format\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15848,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15848},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66fbd8e1-f6af-4fc8-ab9d-b0891d1fb9fd","uuid":"29b39795-1e8e-4aa9-9b29-adeb391b8fef"}
